/github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/8953 about SkinnedMesh, I've been getting multiple issues reported on my viewer (https://github.com/donmccurdy/three-gltf-viewer/issues/147) because the viewport (determined with `Box3().setFromObject(...)`) does not factor in skinning deformations. Those deformations can be 100x for anything converted from FBX.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure that `geometry.boundingBox` should be any different than it is now, but maybe either Box3 or the Mesh subclasses like InstancedMesh and SkinnedMesh should have some method to provide a better bounding box?","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eSimilar to the conversation in \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"156006440\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/8953\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mrdoob/three.js/pull/8953/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/8953\"\u003e#8953\u003c/a\u003e about SkinnedMesh, I've been getting multiple issues reported on my viewer (\u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"441293209\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/donmccurdy/three-gltf-viewer/issues/147\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/donmccurdy/three-gltf-viewer/issues/147/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/donmccurdy/three-gltf-viewer/issues/147\"\u003edonmccurdy/three-gltf-viewer#147\u003c/a\u003e) because the viewport (determined with \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eBox3().setFromObject(...)\u003c/code\u003e) does not factor in skinning deformations. Those deformations can be 100x for anything converted from FBX.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'm not sure that \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003egeometry.boundingBox\u003c/code\u003e should be any different than it is now, but maybe either Box3 or the Mesh subclasses like InstancedMesh and SkinnedMesh should have some method to provide a better bounding box?\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"7b47a1268aa213072d8ff2ec9d71e098e0d1b2e6430394da0eecb433478e7ecf","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABb4aLSegAqTU3MjIxMDY2Nw==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjIxMDY2Nw==","createdAt":"2020-01-08T19:04:33Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/18334#issuecomment-572210667","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":572210667,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDY2ODUwODQ=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTE5NTA0","login":"errrken"},"number":18334,"locked":false,"databaseId":546685084},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjEyMTY1","login":"Mugen87","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12612165?u=60c08e79904982541c82a1ea2dbb0d781a21820b\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/Mugen87","name":"Michael Herzog"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2020-01-08T19:06:13Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzNDU1ODUzMA==","editor":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjEyMTY1","url":"https://github.com/Mugen87","login":"Mugen87"}},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"I think we have a design problem in the library since bounding volumes not only depend on pure geometry data. Classes like `InstancedMesh` or `SkinnedMesh` needs to be considered in order to compute proper AABBs and bounding spheres.\r\n\r\nWhat bothers me is the fact that `BufferGeometry.boundingBox` and `BufferGeometry.boundingSphere` currently represent more or less useless bounding volumes in certain use cases right now. It would be great to find a solution that avoids this situation. Introducing bounding volumes on object level  (and keeping the ones on geometry level) seems a bit of a workaround to me. Although it would be a pragmatic approach.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI think we have a design problem in the library since bounding volumes not only depend on pure geometry data. Classes like \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eInstancedMesh\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eSkinnedMesh\u003c/code\u003e needs to be considered in order to compute proper AABBs and bounding spheres.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhat bothers me is the fact that \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eBufferGeometry.boundingBox\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eBufferGeometry.boundingSphere\u003c/code\u003e currently represent more or less useless bounding volumes in certain use cases right now. It would be great to find a solution that avoids this situation. Introducing bounding volumes on object level  (and keeping the ones on geometry level) seems a bit of a workaround to me. Although it would be a pragmatic approach.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"e129bac1012ade0f4f2e56d0006c7fd57df6c4a3d4a87531ab42ebf6cfdc6e96","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABb4gps8AAqTU3MjM1NTA0NA==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjM1NTA0NA==","createdAt":"2020-01-09T02:37:12Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/18334#issuecomment-572355044","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":572355044,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDY2ODUwODQ=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTE5NTA0","login":"errrken"},"number":18334,"locked":false,"databaseId":546685084},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNDIwMA==","login":"gkjohnson","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/734200?u=f169e56702743d90524c3bb0cc2c17f57f9b7aca\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/gkjohnson","name":"Garrett Johnson"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"\u003e Classes like InstancedMesh or SkinnedMesh needs to be considered in order to compute proper AABBs and bounding spheres.\r\n\r\nI agree -- there are cases even with just a mesh where being able to specify the bounding volume per-object rather than per-geometry would be beneficial. Materials can change the apparent bounds of geometry, as well, with custom vertex shaders, instancing, and displacement maps (which I also think don't work correctly at the moment).\r\n\r\nI still think it's valuable to store the bounding volume on the geometry, though, to share the volume instances. Maybe the responsibility of checking for frustum intersection should shift to the objects? Should the Mesh class define an `intersectsFrustum` function that can be implemented by derivative classes? I think this would help with the problems mentioned here. Here's a simple example:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nMesh.prototype.intersectsFrustum = function ( frustum ) {\r\n\r\n  var geometry = this.geometry;\r\n  var box = this.boundingBox || geometry.boundingBox;\r\n  return frustum.intersectsBox( box );\r\n\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis would allow a bounding box to optionally be set on the Mesh to account for cases where the material changes the visual bounds of the shape. Of course raycasting would also have to be updated to support custom intersections if desired but that's already override-able.","bodyHTML":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eClasses like InstancedMesh or SkinnedMesh needs to be considered in order to compute proper AABBs and bounding spheres.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI agree -- there are cases even with just a mesh where being able to specify the bounding volume per-object rather than per-geometry would be beneficial. Materials can change the apparent bounds of geometry, as well, with custom vertex shaders, instancing, and displacement maps (which I also think don't work correctly at the moment).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI still think it's valuable to store the bounding volume on the geometry, though, to share the volume instances. Maybe the responsibility of checking for frustum intersection should shift to the objects? Should the Mesh class define an \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eintersectsFrustum\u003c/code\u003e function that can be implemented by derivative classes? I think this would help with the problems mentioned here. Here's a simple example:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"Mesh.prototype.intersectsFrustum = function ( frustum ) {\n\n  var geometry = this.geometry;\n  var box = this.boundingBox || geometry.boundingBox;\n  return frustum.intersectsBox( box );\n\n}\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003eMesh\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eprototype\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eintersectsFrustum\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003efunction\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003efrustum\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003evar\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003egeometry\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003ethis\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003egeometry\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003evar\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003ebox\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003ethis\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eboundingBox\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e||\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003egeometry\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eboundingBox\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003efrustum\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eintersectsBox\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s1\"\u003ebox\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis would allow a bounding box to optionally be set on the Mesh to account for cases where the material changes the visual bounds of the shape. Of course raycasting would also have to be updated to support custom intersections if desired but that's already override-able.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"20acc432a8d571049456982f966cf6f8a5c9abb4bd853c3aec28878dd2a432dc","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":2,"nodes":[{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5Mjc5NTE=","login":"sciecode","name":"Guilherme Avila","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3927951?s=64\u0026u=6fe77c9fcb496e961b88eab97563e709f8470336\u0026v=4"},{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MzYyMDg0","login":"webglzhang","name":null,"avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35362084?s=64\u0026u=f71d4beab297e9ee10409c946c41d522fbf01e58\u0026v=4"}]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABb4mmdGgAqTU3MjQ3MzE3Mw==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjQ3MzE3Mw==","createdAt":"2020-01-09T09:33:05Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/18334#issuecomment-572473173","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":572473173,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SX