:"https://github.com/webglzhang","name":null},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"Actually,I do some tries about InstancedMesh's boudingBox and boundingSpere. In my program,I make two bounding that one represents geometry data and other represents the mesh's real volume. I use mesh's real volume to  render sort ,which make transparent rendering isn‘t  right in some cases. I think maybe the method of sorting return Z should also be encapsulated under the subclass of mesh, such as instancedmesh, to make correct calculation and sorting according to different situations.  These are just some of my thoughts,I hope useful.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eActually,I do some tries about InstancedMesh's boudingBox and boundingSpere. In my program,I make two bounding that one represents geometry data and other represents the mesh's real volume. I use mesh's real volume to  render sort ,which make transparent rendering isn‘t  right in some cases. I think maybe the method of sorting return Z should also be encapsulated under the subclass of mesh, such as instancedmesh, to make correct calculation and sorting according to different situations.  These are just some of my thoughts,I hope useful.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"90887fb9bc765e48c02558ebf71030ca4b06b8b3f13e0d901d7774a6503e482a","viewerCanUpdate":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1NzYyMDE=","name":"three.js","owner":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","login":"mrdoob","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob"},"isPrivate":false,"viewerCanCreateIssues":false,"slashCommandsEnabled":false,"nameWithOwner":"mrdoob/three.js","databaseId":576201},"reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MzYyMDg0","login":"webglzhang","name":null,"avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35362084?s=64\u0026u=f71d4beab297e9ee10409c946c41d522fbf01e58\u0026v=4"}]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}]}},{"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABb86Tx4gAqTU3NzMyOTAzOQ==","node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NzMyOTAzOQ==","createdAt":"2020-01-22T18:46:29Z","url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/18334#issuecomment-577329039","isHidden":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":null,"databaseId":577329039,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDY2ODUwODQ=","author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTE5NTA0","login":"errrken"},"number":18334,"locked":false,"databaseId":546685084},"author":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNDIwMA==","login":"gkjohnson","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/734200?u=f169e56702743d90524c3bb0cc2c17f57f9b7aca\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/gkjohnson","name":"Garrett Johnson"},"authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":"2020-01-22T19:21:38Z","lastUserContentEdit":{"id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDM0MjE2MTEzMw==","editor":{"__typename":"User","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNDIwMA==","url":"https://github.com/gkjohnson","login":"gkjohnson"}},"pinnedBy":null,"body":"@Mugen87 \r\n\r\n\u003e I'm not sure about the best design right now. This needs some experimenting and studying. I think it's also worth to check how other engines solve this issue.\r\n\r\nI can appreciate that. I do think it's worth noting that the design pattern chosen for `raycast` affords the type of flexibility we're talking about here, though. Because it's defined on `Object3D` rather than `Ray` the object has control over how to perform the raycasting and handle dependencies on material, shader, and render primitive. We'd be running into a similar situation if instead of `Object3D.raycast` we used `Ray.intersectObject`, I think. The `Frustum.intersectsObject` API feels a little inconsistent at the moment.\r\n\r\n_Edit:_ `Box3.setFromObject` likely suffers from similar issues.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Mugen87/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Mugen87\"\u003e@Mugen87\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'm not sure about the best design right now. This needs some experimenting and studying. I think it's also worth to check how other engines solve this issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI can appreciate that. I d