<p dir="auto">What bothers me is the fact that <code class="notranslate">BufferGeometry.boundingBox</code> and <code class="notranslate">BufferGeometry.boundingSphere</code> currently represent more or less useless bounding volumes in certain use cases right now. It would be great to find a solution that avoids this situation. Introducing bounding volumes on object level  (and keeping the ones on geometry level) seems a bit of a workaround to me. Although it would be a pragmatic approach.</p></div></div><div role="toolbar" aria-label="Reactions" class="d-flex gap-1 flex-wrap"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li data-wrapper-timeline-id="MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjM1NTA0NA=="><div class="timelineElement__l_1Q03 nonLeadingElement_inlineAvatars__g_btmU"><div class="Box__9aTioE"><div data-testid="timeline-divider-MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjM1NTA0NA==" class="Box__swapE6 Box_inlineAvatars__OXEjSV"><div data-testid="timeline-divider-connector" class="Box_1__gSBsk4"></div><div class="Box_2__t0-6Om"></div></div><div data-timeline-event-id="MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjM1NTA0NA==" data-highlighted-event="false" class="shared__KSUE2D major__A5_AyP" data-testid="timeline-row-border-MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjM1NTA0NA=="><div class="react-issue-comment IssueCommentLayout__fNsTnn"><div data-testid="comment-viewer-outer-box-MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MjM1NTA0NA==" class="IssueCommentContent__ViXx9n"><div id="issuecomment-572355044" data-testid="comment-header" class="ActivityHeaderContainer__sf0_ID containerBase__VGAID6 containerForceInlineAvatarPadding__S4YfhL"><div class="activityHeader__V45NcJ ActivityHeaderGridLayout__Ip6-X-"><h3 class="sr-only">gkjohnson<!-- --> <!-- -->commented<!-- --> <relative-time data-component="RelativeTime">on<!-- --> <!-- -->Jan 9, 2020<!-- --> </relative-time></h3><div class="AvatarContainer__ybjZo9"><a class="avatarLink__sqWzwe prc-Link-Link-9ZwDx" data-component="Link" href="/gkjohnson" aria-label="@gkjohnson&#x27;s profile"><img data-compo